From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael J. Ruhl" <michael.j.ruhl@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:18:03 -0700
Subject: [Temp] drm/xe/vsec: Update VSEC probe order

Both debugfs and hwmon access the PMT data area before PMT is
initialized.

Hardwired offset usage allows this to work by accident.
Upcoming changes will break this usage.

Re-order the probe steps to initialize VSEC before the other
features are initialized.

Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi <rodrigo.vivi@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Michael J. Ruhl <michael.j.ruhl@intel.com>
(backported from https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/series/160717/#rev12)
Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
index 238aa0772..845a6b711 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
@@ -1086,6 +1086,8 @@ int xe_device_probe(struct xe_device *xe)
 	if (err)
 		goto err_unregister_display;
 
+	xe_vsec_init(xe);
+
 	xe_debugfs_register(xe);
 
 	err = xe_hwmon_register(xe);
@@ -1099,8 +1101,6 @@ int xe_device_probe(struct xe_device *xe)
 	for_each_gt(gt, xe, id)
 		xe_gt_sanitize_freq(gt);
 
-	xe_vsec_init(xe);
-
 	err = xe_sriov_init_late(xe);
 	if (err)
 		goto err_unregister_display;
-- 
